<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29090" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĭmas</span></b> , antis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μίμας</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A mountain range in Ionia, opposite the Isle of
				Chios, a branch of Mount Tmolus, still called Mimas</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29,
				31, § 118</span></i>; Ov M. 2, 222; <i><span class="en">Luc. 7,
			451</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 16, 13</span></i>, a, 2; <i><span class="en">id.
				Fragm. p. 580</span></i> Orell.; <i><span class="en">Amm. 31, 14,
				8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A giant</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Typhoeus et validus Mimas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 4, 53</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sil. 4, 278</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A Trojan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mimanta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 702</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
